CLASSES AND JVM:
-> class is used to create objects
-> Imagine a situation where you want an table desk and approached a carpenter to make one for you.
-> and now the carpenter asks you to give the design or some technical details inorder to make one so
   here comes the concept called class where class behaves as a blueprint to create an object(make one table object).
-> so in programming it follows same concept and the object will be created by the JVM in Java
the steps involves like below;
                                   the class will gives the blueprint on how the object should be created.
                                                                       |
                                         the class file will now compiled to create a byte code
                                                                       |
                                          that byte code goes into the JVM and creates the object.
